// Phase 0.5 regression: a genuinely UNSUPPORTED construct must HARD-FAIL the build, not silently corrupt
// the binary. Before Phase 0.5, klower's lowFail printed "unsupported construct" to stdout and RETURNED 0,
// so lowering continued and emitted a garbage binary that "built" with exit 0. Now lowFail emits an error
// Diagnostic to stderr and calls __abort() → non-zero exit, no binary written.
//
// The construct below — assigning into a String index (`s[i] = v`) — is lowered by klower's lowerAssignInto
// straight to lowFail("cannot store into an immutable String index"). The gate compiles this with
// `--no-check` (so it reaches the lowerer, not just the checker) and asserts a non-zero exit + no output
// binary + a stderr diagnostic. If a future phase makes String index-store supported, swap this fixture for
// another still-unsupported construct rather than deleting the assertion.
fun main(): Int {
  var s = "hello"
  s[0] = 88
  return 0
}
